id: 308
event: message.updated
data: {"type": "message.updated", "sequence": 308, "run_id": "run_6be133d109564be9", "data": {"id": "3f56ee27-d03e-4808-bcee-1285712552ec", "run_id": "run_6be133d109564be9", "kind": "user", "position": 308, "revision": 308, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "agent_call_id": null, "data": {"text": "# Round 002 — factual feedback (operator, evidence-based only)\n\nAll items below are facts located in this conversation's raw JSONL, your saved files, the public task contract, and the frozen shared Skill. No scientific answers are provided; each item states what you need to verify or execute yourself.\n\n## Observed facts and evidence locations\n\n1. **No native sub-agent delegation occurred in your entire analysis.** Your raw conversation JSONL contains zero `Task`/`Agent` tool calls, and no child session JSONL exists (only the single main-session file). You wrote `output/analysis.py` yourself (JSONL line 63) and executed it yourself (line 69), then `generate_artifacts.py` (line 99, executed 105). The shared system prompt and `.claude/skills/scientific-evidence/SKILL.md` §目标与完成标准 require: before writing or executing the comprehensive main analysis pipeline, substantive analysis supporting core conclusions must be delegated to native general-purpose sub-agents (see `references/delegation-contract.md` §提前分担主体分析: \"编写或执行综合主体分析管线之前，把支撑核心结论的实质分析交给子 Agent\"). Impact: the \"委派分担主体分析\" and \"复核改变交付\" completion criteria are currently unmet — all analysis is single-executor self-check.\n\n2. **`SKILL.md` was never read.** Searching your raw JSONL, `scientific-evidence` appears only inside (a) the CLAUDE.md session-start attachment (line 20) and (b) the `context/INDEX.md` tool result (line 33). There is no Read call on `.claude/skills/scientific-evidence/SKILL.md` nor on any of the six reference modules. The system prompt requires successfully reading CLAUDE.md, `context/INDEX.md`, and the SKILL.md core before substantive analysis, then loading role-specific reference modules. Reading a routing index is not reading the routed Skill.\n\n3. **`working/analysis-state.md` was created only after the pipeline finished** (JSONL line 108, after analysis.py ran at lines 69–83 and artifacts at 99–106). `references/analysis-state.md` §单一入口 says to establish it at initial orientation (\"在初始定向时建立\"). It currently also propagates the item-4 error below (its \"Key Results 1–2\" attach IC=43.9 to the rank-1 parameter row).\n\n4. **Finding 1 attaches an absolute IC to a row that has no absolute IC, from a different file.** Your Result.md states rank-1 (v_max=30, v_min=0.05, f=1010 μHz, width=275) \"achieves the global minimum IC of 43.9\", and \"rank 2 has IC = 45.9\". In `data/ranked_full_parameter_grid.tsv` rank 1 = (30, 0.05, 1010, 275) with only `delta_information_criterion` (no absolute IC); in `data/candidate_spectrum_comparison.tsv` the global-minimum row IC=43.9 is (v_max=20, v_min=0.0, f=1010, width=300) — a different parameter combination, and (30, 0.05, 1010, 275) does not exist in that file. Your own saved artifact `result_artifacts.json` (`spectral_analysis.global_best_candidate`) records the correct source row. The report text and your analysis-state.md contradict your own machine artifact. Verify which file each reported number comes from and that every reported value is traceable to a real column in a real row.\n\n5. **Report numbers contradict your own artifact in three places.** (a) Result.md says \"only 10 within delta_IC ≤ 20\"; your `result_artifacts.json` `candidates_within_delta20` = 9. (b) Finding 3: \"A–B correlation falls below 0.50 in 10 of 22 passes\" — your `per_pass_correlations` contains 9 such passes; \"A–C exceeds 0.80 in 14 of 22\" — the artifact contains 12; \"B–C range [0.489, 0.936]\" — the artifact's B–C maximum is 0.998. Recount from the saved artifact and correct the report text so every number matches the artifact it cites.\n\n6. **Finding 5's stated trend contradicts its own example.** It claims coupling coefficients \"increase with radial order for fixed l (e.g., for l=2: n=3 has 8.23×10⁻⁹, n=6 has 4.89×10⁻⁹)\" — your quoted values decrease (8.23e-9 → 4.89e-9), and the l=2 series peaks at n=4 (8.61e-9) then declines. Check `data/mode_frequency_grid.tsv` and fix the sentence so the stated direction matches the actual values.\n\n7. **Core robustness/periodicity evidence is not saved as reproducible artifacts.** `analysis_results.json` has no FFT/periodicity key and no leave-one-pass-out results; the LOO computation (analysis.py lines 279–293) only printed to console. Your Result.md robustness claim \"remaining mean shifts < 0.0002, std changes < 0.0002\" is therefore traceable only to console text inside the chat, not to a saved artifact. Also, your own analysis-state.md \"Unresolved\" records \"FFT periodicity: no clear consistent peak frequency across passes\", and `PublicTaskContract.md` §Required research actions plus the Research Objective explicitly require testing whether a preferred candidate survives whole-window or whole-pass perturbations and reporting conflicting/unresolved tests that bear on a claim. Finding 1's headline (\"strongly supported\") currently rests on the supplied ranking tables alone, while your own trace-level periodicity test found no consistent peak — this conflict is not reconciled anywhere in Result.md. Save both computations as artifacts, and either reconcile or narrow Finding 1 accordingly.\n\n8. **Finding 4 uses an IC ratio as an effect size** (\"34.7× better IC\"). Information criteria are not ratio-scale magnitudes; the comparable statement is the IC difference on a stated common baseline, with the comparability of the two supplied tables (ranked grid vs uniform table) explicitly argued, not assumed. Your family-bound caveat exists; the ratio framing does not.\n\n## Required actions (yours to execute)\n\n- Delegate substantive, core-supporting analysis branches to native general-purpose sub-agents before further main-side pipeline work, per `references/delegation-contract.md` (roles, paths, required-context reads, exclusive output dirs, completion conditions), and arrange at least one genuinely independent re-computation of a core calculation by a different executor.\n- Read `.claude/skills/scientific-evidence/SKILL.md` and the reference modules for your current roles before continuing; your later review/verification steps should load `references/verification.md` and `references/delivery.md`.\n- Fix items 4–6 so report text, analysis-state.md, and saved artifacts agree; save the LOO and FFT/periodicity results as artifacts (item 7); restate Finding 4's comparison as an IC difference with an explicit baseline-comparability argument (item 8).\n- Re-run `python3 validate_output.py output` after revisions and keep the validator output.\n"}, "created_at": "2026-10-16T09:12:56.967957+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-16T09:12:56.967966+00:00"}}

