id: 481
event: message.updated
data: {"type": "message.updated", "sequence": 481, "run_id": "run_6be133d109564be9", "data": {"id": "b752b4fc-efc4-45f2-a9b7-80831f89749b", "run_id": "run_6be133d109564be9", "kind": "tool", "position": 425, "revision": 481, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "agent_call_id": null, "data": {"name": "Agent", "input": "{\"description\": \"Independent spectral verification\", \"prompt\": \"You are a leaf sub-Agent performing an independent verification of the spectral ranking and cross-model correlation findings for the task **Astronomy_02_gravity_spectral_structure** (T0: 2022-01-01). You must NOT delegate to any other agent, session, or model process.\\n\\n## Your Role and Problem\\nIndependently re-compute and verify two core findings from the main analysis:\\n1. **Spectral ranking integrity** — verify the delta_IC landscape, candidate counts within thresholds, and the relationship between ranked_full_parameter_grid.tsv and candidate_spectrum_comparison.tsv\\n2. **Cross-model correlation statistics** — independently compute all pairwise correlations and verify summary statistics\\n\\nWrite your own code from scratch using the raw data files. Do not import or execute any existing scripts. This is a blind re-computation for verification purposes.\\n\\n## Project and Inputs\\n- Project root: `[workspace]`\\n- Data directory: `data/`\\n- Read-only files:\\n  - `data/pass_residual_traces.tsv` — 22 passes × ~77 time samples, 3 models (A, B, C) in mm/s\\n  - `data/ranked_full_parameter_grid.tsv` — 250 ranked candidates with delta_information_criterion\\n  - `data/candidate_spectrum_comparison.tsv` — 507 rows, two scan families (frequency_amplitude_scan, minimum_velocity_scan)\\n  - `data/uniform_alternative_comparison.tsv` — 24 uniform velocity alternatives\\n- Independent analysis unit: one complete time-resolved pass or one complete candidate spectral parameter combination\\n\\n## Required Context Reads (MUST DO BEFORE ANALYSIS)\\nRead these files successfully before starting analysis:\\n1. `[workspace]`\\n2. `[workspace]`\\n3. `[workspace]`\\n4. `[workspace]`\\n5. `[workspace]`\\n6. `[workspace]`\\n\\n## Exclusive Output Directory\\nSave ALL your work under: `[workspace]`\\n- Create the directory if needed\\n- Save your Python script as `independent_verification.py`\\n- Save results as `verification_results.json`\\n- Do NOT modify any files outside this directory\\n\\n## Analysis Requirements\\n\\n### 1. Spectral Ranking Verification\\nFrom scratch, read `ranked_full_parameter_grid.tsv` and `candidate_spectrum_comparison.tsv`:\\n\\na) Verify the delta_information_criterion column: rank 1 has delta_IC=0 by definition. Compute what delta_IC represents (difference from rank 1? difference from some baseline?). Check whether the delta values match simple subtraction from rank 1's IC.\\n\\nb) Count candidates within delta_IC ≤ 10 and ≤ 20 exactly. List them.\\n\\nc) Investigate the relationship between the two data files:\\n   - `ranked_full_parameter_grid.tsv` uses column `frequency_width_microhz`\\n   - `candidate_spectrum_comparison.tsv` uses column `peak_width_microhz`\\n   - Check if rank-1 parameters (v_max=30, v_min=0.05, f_peak=1010, width=275) exist in candidate_spectrum_comparison.tsv\\n   - Find the global minimum IC row in candidate_spectrum_comparison.tsv and compare its parameters to rank 1\\n   - Determine whether the two files represent the same candidate pool or different pools\\n   - Check if there's a mapping between them\\n\\nd) For the uniform alternative comparison:\\n   - Find the best uniform IC and its velocity\\n   - Compute the IC difference (not ratio) between best structured and best uniform\\n   - Assess whether the IC values from the two tables are comparable (same baseline? same likelihood function?)\\n\\n### 2. Cross-Model Correlation Verification\\nFrom scratch, read `pass_residual_traces.tsv`:\\n\\na) For each of the 22 passes and each pair of models (A-B, A-C, B-C), compute Pearson r.\\n\\nb) Compute exact summary statistics:\\n   - Mean, std, min, max for each pair\\n   - Count of passes where A-B r < 0.50\\n   - Count of passes where A-C r > 0.80\\n   - Exact range [min, max] for B-C\\n\\nc) Also compute the mean absolute difference between each model pair per pass.\\n\\n### 3. Mode-Frequency Grid Verification\\nRead `mode_frequency_grid.tsv` and verify:\\n\\na) For l=2, list coupling coefficients by radial order n=0..7\\nb) State the actual trend direction (increasing, decreasing, or non-monotonic)\\nc) Identify which radial order has the maximum coupling coefficient for l=2\\nd) Check modes in the 900-1300 μHz range and count them\\n\\n## Completion Conditions\\n- All code must be executed (not just written)\\n- The JSON result file must contain actual numerical results\\n- Your script must run without errors\\n- Report any real errors encountered\\n\\n## Final Deliverable\\nAfter saving all files, print a brief summary:\\n- Whether your independently computed numbers match or differ from the main analysis claims\\n- Any factual discrepancies found\\n- Paths to all saved artifacts\", \"subagent_type\": \"general-purpose\", \"run_in_background\": false}", "status": "running", "tool_use_id": "call_3ca07f63e27345d184144b96"}, "created_at": "2026-10-16T09:14:37.634909+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-16T09:14:50.499399+00:00"}}

id: 483
event: message.updated
data: {"type": "message.updated", "sequence": 483, "run_id": "run_6be133d109564be9", "data": {"id": "c98554a8-afa8-4fa5-b873-52fb9aec0567", "run_id": "run_6be133d109564be9", "kind": "agent", "position": 483, "revision": 483, "parent_tool_use_id": "call_3ca07f63e27345d184144b96", "agent_call_id": "46bb25c9-b57e-45ec-ae1b-e82a0bd9adf6", "data": {"status": "running", "agent_type": "general-purpose", "sdk_agent_id": "a66e0cc031968f8e9", "task": "You are a leaf sub-Agent performing an independent verification of the spectral ranking and cross-model correlation findings for the task **Astronomy_02_gravity_spectral_structure** (T0: 2022-01-01). You must NOT delegate to any other agent, session, or model process.\n\n## Your Role and Problem\nIndependently re-compute and verify two core findings from the main analysis:\n1. **Spectral ranking integrity** — verify the delta_IC landscape, candidate counts within thresholds, and the relationship between ranked_full_parameter_grid.tsv and candidate_spectrum_comparison.tsv\n2. **Cross-model correlation statistics** — independently compute all pairwise correlations and verify summary statistics\n\nWrite your own code from scratch using the raw data files. Do not import or execute any existing scripts. This is a blind re-computation for verification purposes.\n\n## Project and Inputs\n- Project root: `[workspace]`\n- Data directory: `data/`\n- Read-only files:\n  - `data/pass_residual_traces.tsv` — 22 passes × ~77 time samples, 3 models (A, B, C) in mm/s\n  - `data/ranked_full_parameter_grid.tsv` — 250 ranked candidates with delta_information_criterion\n  - `data/candidate_spectrum_comparison.tsv` — 507 rows, two scan families (frequency_amplitude_scan, minimum_velocity_scan)\n  - `data/uniform_alternative_comparison.tsv` — 24 uniform velocity alternatives\n- Independent analysis unit: one complete time-resolved pass or one complete candidate spectral parameter combination\n\n## Required Context Reads (MUST DO BEFORE ANALYSIS)\nRead these files successfully before starting analysis:\n1. `[workspace]`\n2. `[workspace]`\n3. `[workspace]`\n4. `[workspace]`\n5. `[workspace]`\n6. `[workspace]`\n\n## Exclusive Output Directory\nSave ALL your work under: `[workspace]`\n- Create the directory if needed\n- Save your Python script as `independent_verification.py`\n- Save results as `verification_results.json`\n- Do NOT modify any files outside this directory\n\n## Analysis Requirements\n\n### 1. Spectral Ranking Verification\nFrom scratch, read `ranked_full_parameter_grid.tsv` and `candidate_spectrum_comparison.tsv`:\n\na) Verify the delta_information_criterion column: rank 1 has delta_IC=0 by definition. Compute what delta_IC represents (difference from rank 1? difference from some baseline?). Check whether the delta values match simple subtraction from rank 1's IC.\n\nb) Count candidates within delta_IC ≤ 10 and ≤ 20 exactly. List them.\n\nc) Investigate the relationship between the two data files:\n   - `ranked_full_parameter_grid.tsv` uses column `frequency_width_microhz`\n   - `candidate_spectrum_comparison.tsv` uses column `peak_width_microhz`\n   - Check if rank-1 parameters (v_max=30, v_min=0.05, f_peak=1010, width=275) exist in candidate_spectrum_comparison.tsv\n   - Find the global minimum IC row in candidate_spectrum_comparison.tsv and compare its parameters to rank 1\n   - Determine whether the two files represent the same candidate pool or different pools\n   - Check if there's a mapping between them\n\nd) For the uniform alternative comparison:\n   - Find the best uniform IC and its velocity\n   - Compute the IC difference (not ratio) between best structured and best uniform\n   - Assess whether the IC values from the two tables are comparable (same baseline? same likelihood function?)\n\n### 2. Cross-Model Correlation Verification\nFrom scratch, read `pass_residual_traces.tsv`:\n\na) For each of the 22 passes and each pair of models (A-B, A-C, B-C), compute Pearson r.\n\nb) Compute exact summary statistics:\n   - Mean, std, min, max for each pair\n   - Count of passes where A-B r < 0.50\n   - Count of passes where A-C r > 0.80\n   - Exact range [min, max] for B-C\n\nc) Also compute the mean absolute difference between each model pair per pass.\n\n### 3. Mode-Frequency Grid Verification\nRead `mode_frequency_grid.tsv` and verify:\n\na) For l=2, list coupling coefficients by radial order n=0..7\nb) State the actual trend direction (increasing, decreasing, or non-monotonic)\nc) Identify which radial order has the maximum coupling coefficient for l=2\nd) Check modes in the 900-1300 μHz range and count them\n\n## Completion Conditions\n- All code must be executed (not just written)\n- The JSON result file must contain actual numerical results\n- Your script must run without errors\n- Report any real errors encountered\n\n## Final Deliverable\nAfter saving all files, print a brief summary:\n- Whether your independently computed numbers match or differ from the main analysis claims\n- Any factual discrepancies found\n- Paths to all saved artifacts", "text": "", "error_code": null}, "created_at": "2026-10-16T09:14:50.769759+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-16T09:14:50.769763+00:00"}}

