act summary statistics:\n   - Mean, std, min, max for each pair\n   - Count of passes where A-B r < 0.50\n   - Count of passes where A-C r > 0.80\n   - Exact range [min, max] for B-C\n\nc) Also compute the mean absolute difference between each model pair per pass.\n\n### 3. Mode-Frequency Grid Verification\nRead `mode_frequency_grid.tsv` and verify:\n\na) For l=2, list coupling coefficients by radial order n=0..7\nb) State the actual trend direction (increasing, decreasing, or non-monotonic)\nc) Identify which radial order has the maximum coupling coefficient for l=2\nd) Check modes in the 900-1300 μHz range and count them\n\n## Completion Conditions\n- All code must be executed (not just written)\n- The JSON result file must contain actual numerical results\n- Your script must run without errors\n- Report any real errors encountered\n\n## Final Deliverable\nAfter saving all files, print a brief summary:\n- Whether your independently computed numbers match or differ from the main analysis claims\n- Any factual discrepancies found\n- Paths to all saved artifacts", "text": "Both files are saved. Here is the verification report:\n\n---\n\n## Independent Verification Report\n\n### Files Saved\n- `[workspace]` (source script)\n- `[workspace]` (full numerical results, 529 lines)\n\n### Key Findings\n\n**1. Spectral Ranking Verification**\n\n- **delta_IC definition**: Confirmed rank 1 has delta_IC=0 by definition. The delta values increase monotonically with rank. However, the delta_IC in `ranked_full_parameter_grid.tsv` does NOT correspond to `IC - global_min_ic` from `candidate_spectrum_comparison.tsv` -- all 29 overlapping entries show a constant offset of 43.9 (the global minimum IC), meaning `delta_IC = IC_candidate - IC_rank1_in_ranked_table`, where the ranked table uses a different baseline than the candidate comparison table.\n\n- **Threshold counts**: Exactly **4 candidates** have delta_IC <= 10 (ranks 1-4), and **9 candidates** have delta_IC <= 20 (ranks 1-9). These numbers are exact and reproducible.\n\n- **File relationship**: The two files represent **overlapping but different candidate pools**. `ranked_full_parameter_grid.tsv` has 250 unique combos; `candidate_spectrum_comparison.tsv` has 507 unique combos; only 29 overlap. Rank 1 params (v_max=30, v_min=0.05, f_peak=1010, width=275) do NOT exist in `candidate_spectrum_comparison.tsv`. The global minimum IC in the candidate file (43.9) belongs to a different parameter set (v_max=20, v_min=0, f_peak=1010, width=300).\n\n- **Uniform alternative**: Best uniform velocity is 0.1 cm/s with IC=1522.1. The best structured IC is 43.9. The IC difference is -1478.2 (structured is much lower/better). The ranges overlap at the top end (both reach ~13553.2), suggesting they may share the same likelihood framework but different model structures.\n\n**2. Cross-Model Correlation Verification**\n\nComputed from 22 passes across all pairs:\n\n| Pair | Mean r | Std | Min | Max |\n|------|--------|-----|-----|-----|\n| A-B | 0.5730 | 0.1837 | 0.2528 | 0.9940 |\n| A-C | 0.8097 | 0.1154 | 0.5748 | 0.9973 |\n| B-C | 0.7832 | 0.1323 | 0.4892 | 0.9980 |\n\n- Passes where A-B r < 0.50: **9 out of 22**\n- Passes where A-C r > 0.80: **12 out of 22**\n- B-C range: **[0.4892, 0.9980]**\n\nMean absolute differences also computed per pair.\n\n**3. Mode-Frequency Grid Verification**\n\n- For l=2, coupling coefficients by radial order n=0..7: 2.06e-09, 5.59e-09, 6.07e-09, 8.23e-09, 8.61e-09, 7.27e-09, 4.89e-09, 2.56e-09\n- Trend: **non-monotonic** (increases from n=0 to n=4, then decreases through n=7)\n- Maximum coupling for l=2: **n=4** with coefficient 8.61e-09\n- Modes in 900-1300 microHz range: **16 modes** across angular degrees l=2 through l=8\n\n### Discrepancies Noted\n\nThe most significant finding is that `ranked_full_parameter_grid.tsv` and `candidate_spectrum_comparison.tsv` use **different candidate pools** (only 29/250 overlap), which means any direct cross-referencing between them requires careful handling. The delta_IC values cannot be directly compared to the information_criterion values in the candidate file without accounting for different baselines.", "error_code": null}, "created_at": "2026-10-16T09:14:50.769759+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-16T09:20:20.779170+00:00"}}

